19319b2afa1d8bb986682f7effb9&node=euler.theorem-1.1&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=cb411968cba7fc485f109c1520e67d42f66919319b2afa1d8bb986682f7effb9&node=euler.theorem-1.1&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=cb411968cba7fc485f109c1520e67d42f66919319b2afa1d8bb986682f7effb9&view=arguments&node=euler.theorem-1.1&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=cb411968cba7fc485f109c1520e67d42f66919319b2afa1d8bb986682f7effb9&ref=sha256%3Aa36e91bc5016ddb9bc06c5aa03801b802710f25448aebbdca71e3fb4b5730c68%2Fnodes%2Feuler.theorem-1.1","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A result as the authors number it. Its links to the Lean were made with AI for Proof Reader and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.euler.theorem-1.1"],"evidence_ids":["link.euler.theorem-1.1"],"id":"euler.theorem-1.1","kind":"goal","label":"Theorem 1.1","locator":"Theorem 1.1, Section 1","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Theorem 1.1.** There is an odd divergence-free $u_0\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)$ whose maximal classical solution $u$ of (1.1) is smooth and odd on $\\mathbb T^3\\times[0,T_*)$ for a finite $T_*>0$, and satisfies $$\\begin{equation}\n \\int_0^{T_*}\\|\\nabla u(t)\\|_{L^\\infty}\\,\\mathrm dt=\\infty,\n \\qquad\n \\int_0^{T_*}\\|\\operatorname{curl}u(t)\\|_{L^\\infty}\\,\\mathrm dt=\\infty. \\tag{1.2}\n\\end{equation}$$ Moreover, $$\\begin{equation}\n \\sup_{0\\le t<T_*}\\|u(t)\\|_{L^\\infty}<\\infty,\n \\qquad \\lim_{t\\uparrow T_*}|\\operatorname{curl}u(t,0)|=\\infty. \\tag{1.3}\n\\end{equation}$$ For every compact $K\\subset\\mathbb T^3\\setminus\\{0\\}$ and every integer $m\\ge0$, both $u(t)$ and $\\partial_tu(t)$ converge in $C^m(K)$ as $t\\uparrow T_*$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:a36e91bc5016ddb9bc06c5aa03801b802710f25448aebbdca71e3fb4b5730c68/nodes/euler.theorem-1.1","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:a36e91bc5016dd